  "body": "## What changed\nA swarf raster line used to turn upright on its exit rise, which forced an air link (retract, swing, re-plunge) at every raster end. Now, where it is proved safe, the rise posts as a **rapid that keeps the lying pose the line cut with**; the pose carries through the clearance rapid and the next line plunges under that same pose, so there is no head swing at all. New `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/stamp_rise.rs` decides it; `stamp.rs` calls it during posing. Every condition must hold, otherwise the rise stays the old upright feed and the existing link law handles the turn:\n- a feed going straight up Z with no XY travel;\n- the program has already leaned, and the held pose is a lean not below level;\n- the end of the rise is in air (beyond the contact band);\n- the ball never gets closer to the part on the way up than at the start (the same floor the link retract uses);\n- the held pose's flank is proved clear (`flank_clear`) at every half-radius sample up the rise.\n\nThe ball travels exactly the path the plan already gave it; only the flank differs, and it is checked. The rotaries don't move during the rapid. A rapid claims no contact, so the posed-contact law that flagged #17's in-air posed feed has nothing to judge; the posed-rapid solid law still checks it like every link retract. **No verifier law changed**; the other option (excusing a feed that leaves along the surface normal) was dropped.\n\n## Readings\n`swarf_pose_continuity` was **already red on main** (3 pass / 2 fail) in the same ratchet: the advanced count had drifted to 53 (pin 51) and the advanced full band to 86 (pin 84). This PR brings every count well under the old pins and sets the pins to the new counts:\n\n| run | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| swarf, debug band | 34 | 23 |\n| advanced, debug band | 53 | 34 |\n| swarf, full band | 55 | 44 |\n| advanced, full band | 86 | 67 |\n\n- `swarf_pose_continuity` 6/6 (was 3/5); motion `--lib multiaxis` 57; `swarf_reentry`, `ruling`, `pivot5d` debug all pass; `pivot5d` heavy lane (release, `--ignored`) `the_envelope_reads_every_posed_kind_as_its_plan` passes (an envelope scan #17 left owed).\n- app `operations::swarf_generates_blade_lying_axes_and_verifies_clean` and `advanced_swarf_adds_the_coarse_rungs` verify clean, as do their `_full_band` twins in the ignored lane; app `verify`, `area_controls`, `center_cut_multiaxis`, the swarf `project_roundtrip` test; sim `posed_rapids`, `posed_fixture_midpose` all pass.\n- Quick gate (motion suites): green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n`swarf_pose_continuity::every_raster_exit_rise_is_a_rapid_holding_the_lying_pose` (new; finds no lying rises on the old code), the lowered link ratchets in `swarf_pose_continuity`, and `stamp_rise` unit tests (rapid when the flank is clear; stays a feed when a wall blocks the flank; rejects anything that isn't a straight rise from a lean into air).\n\n## Needs the maintainer's hands (why this stays a draft)\n**Posted swarf G-code changes**: each raster end was retract, swing, re-plunge, then an upright G1 rise; it is now one G0 rise at the lying A/B/C angles, with the lying pose carried through the clearance move. No golden covers swarf output, so none moved. Please run a swarf program through Hub / a real machine (watch the G0 rise at the leaned pose) before marking ready.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/48-swarf-exit-rise.md`.\n\nChangelog: Swarf: each raster line now leaves the blade on a rapid that keeps its lying tool angle instead of turning upright through an air link, so a raster end no longer swings the head (air links 34 to 23 on the test blade)\n\nFixes #48\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
